{"id":"chatcmpl-0b60f023-c118-462e-bb86-416182956d20","object":"chat.completion","created":1795230723,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a visual question-answering task requires distinguishing between two similar findings (e.g., left vs. right laterality), the successful strategy was to query multiple independent expert models, resolve conflicts via a verification step, and confirm with targeted high-magnification ROI inspection. The key insight is that subtle findings often produce model disagreement, so consensus-building across diverse models plus visual confirmation is more reliable than trusting any single source.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Query multiple independent expert models when the finding is subtle or laterality must be determined, since single-model outputs are unreliable for fine-grained distinctions.\",\n    \"When models conflict, insert an explicit verification step that states the conflict and the reasoning risk before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Use targeted ROI cropping and zoom on the anatomically relevant region (e.g., posterior costophrenic angles) to visually confirm subtle findings that models disagree on.\",\n    \"Weight the final answer toward the majority of valid, independent model outputs plus visual confirmation, discarding failed or non-responsive model calls.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"For subtle or lateralized findings, poll several independent vision-language models, then confirm with a zoomed crop of the relevant anatomy; treat model consensus plus visual evidence as the deciding signal.\",\n    \"Ambiguous visual classification\": \"When options differ only by a fine attribute (side, location, grade), gather multiple independent assessments and use a verification step to explicitly reconcile disagreements before answering.\",\n    \"Tool-orchestrated reasoning\": \"Chain specialized tools (expert model, second opinion, ROI crop, verifier) so each step addresses a specific uncertainty; escalate to additional models only when conflicts persist.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether model outputs agree; if not, run a verification step naming the conflict and the anatomical reasoning before finalizing.\",\n    \"Visually inspect a high-magnification crop of the region of interest to corroborate the chosen answer against model consensus.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1154,"total_tokens":1570,"completion_tokens":416,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":1154},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":416}}}